     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals, or 1,700 mg once daily if the intent was a daily total.\n- **Another dose.** For a new start, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily, titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
